  "shuiPhotoTitle1": "The water shop and Shui’s “clean water.”",
  "shuiPhotoTitle2": "Not chubby. Strong.",
  "shuiPhotoTitle3": "Say “I love you” before goodbye.",
  "shuiPhotoText1": "We talked about the shop, and I asked if the family sold water filters. His caregiver said yes. Shui also made a point of saying he was clean water. His name, Shui, means “water.”",
  "shuiPhotoText2": "Shui was quick to say he was strong, not chubby, and that Shunshun was too. This big brother is pretty sure of himself.",
  "shuiPhotoText3": "As we were finishing, Shui still wanted to hear his sister say she loved him. After all the cheeky talk, he wanted their love said out loud.",
  "shuiPhotoAlt1": "Shui wearing a harness and being held by a family member in the shop",
  "shuiPhotoAlt2": "Shui sitting on grass with his mouth open, facing the camera",
  "shuiPhotoAlt3": "Shui resting in his bed against a blue toy",
  "shuiPhotosLabel": "Three moments from Shui’s story",
  "shuiCleanTitle": "A family water shop, and Shui’s very own “clean water” logic.",
  "shuiCleanBody": "At first, I only knew Shui was keeping an eye on the shop. As we chatted, I shared that he said his family sold water. I asked if they sold water filters, and his caregiver said yes. That gave us a clearer picture of life at the shop. Shui also made a point of saying he was clean water. His name means “water,” and he linked it to the family business in his own very serious way. His caregiver explained that he was actually named Shui because he’d been found by a stream. He’d joined the family before they opened the shop. That funny bit of Shui logic became one of the best parts of our chat.",
  "soniaPhotoTitle1": "We can chat from a little distance.",
